<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- karzat: the local half of the hybrid nightly.

     parlament.hu answered its API on the reader's network and served its portal page to the datacenter's
     (August 2026; a probe on 7 November got the API's own 401 from a datacenter, so this may no longer hold),
     so the sync runs HERE, on the machine whose connection the service accepts. While the AWS account's silent
     45-minute build cap stands (a new-account limit; a support case lifts it), this job runs the WHOLE chain:
     sync, handover to s3://karzat-ops, build, tests, README gate, deploy. It alerts the same SNS topic on
     failure, leaves a local marker, and writes a heartbeat the GitHub watchdog reads. Once the cap is lifted:
     re-enable the karzat-nightly schedule (EventBridge Scheduler, eu-central-1) and run the sync-only mode
     here instead of the refresh-days, handover and sns-topic arguments below.

     caffeinate. The Mac does not stay awake for a job started at 04:10: on 7 November it fell asleep 226
     times between 03:00 and 09:00, waking for a few seconds every quarter of an hour, and the nightly
     advanced only in those slivers. A request that takes 0.2 s awake took 100 to 200 s, and a chain that
     needs 79 minutes awake took between three and a half and seven hours. caffeinate holds a sleep
     assertion for exactly as long as its child runs and releases it when the child exits: -i idle sleep,
     -m disk sleep, -s system sleep, the last only on mains power. On battery, or with the lid shut and no
     external display, the Mac sleeps anyway, and the watchdog is what notices.

     Install:   cp config/hu.ogykarzat.sync.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
                launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/hu.ogykarzat.sync.plist
     Remove:    launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/hu.ogykarzat.sync
     Log:       ~/Library/Logs/karzat-sync.log

     A calendar job the Mac sleeps through fires once on the next wake, so a closed laptop shifts the sync
     rather than losing it; the watchdog turns a sync that stays missing into an email, never into a quietly
     stale site. -->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>hu.ogykarzat.sync</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/usr/bin/caffeinate</string>
        <string>-ims</string>
        <string>/Users/host/.pyenv/versions/3.11.5/bin/python3</string>
        <string>-m</string>
        <string>scripts.nightly</string>
        <string>--profile</string>
        <string>karzat</string>
        <string>--refresh-days</string>
        <string>7</string>
        <string>--handover</string>
        <string>--sns-topic</string>
        <string>arn:aws:sns:eu-central-1:508888023472:karzat-nightly</string>
    </array>
    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/host/Claude - Projects/karzat</string>
    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <dict>
        <key>Hour</key>
        <integer>4</integer>
        <key>Minute</key>
        <integer>10</integer>
    </dict>
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/host/Library/Logs/karzat-sync.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/host/Library/Logs/karzat-sync.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
